<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gannascus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 47</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gannascus was a Germanic leader of the Cananefates who led Chauci raids on the coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Roman Gaul</a> in 47 CE. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tacitus">Tacitus</a> reports that he had earlier served <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> as an auxiliary before deserting. The general Corbulo defeated the raiders at sea and later had Gannascus assassinated, provoking unrest among the Chauci.</p></div>
